keyd-rust-application-mapper(1)

# NAME

keyd-rust-application-mapper - remap keys when window focus changes

# SYNOPSIS

*keyd-rust-application-mapper* [*-d*|*--daemonize*] [*-v*|*--verbose*]

# OPTIONS

*-v, --verbose*
	Print window class and title names for use in the config file.

*-d, --daemonize*
	Run in the background and write output to _~/.config/keyd-rust/app.log_.

# DESCRIPTION

The mapper reads _~/.config/keyd-rust/app.conf_ and applies bindings when a
matching window gets focus. The bindings override _/etc/keyd-rust/\*.conf_.

The config file has the following form:

```
	[<filter>]

	<expression 1>
	<expression 2>
	...
```

_<filter>_ has one of the following forms:

```
	\[<class exp>\]              # Match by window class
	\[<class exp>|<title exp>\]  # Match by class and title
```

Each _<expression>_ is a valid argument to _keyd-rust bind_.
See *Bindings* in *keyd-rust(1)*.

_<class exp>_ and _<title exp>_ match window class and title names.
Use \* as a wildcard. For example, _[gnome|\*find\*]_ matches class _gnome_
with _find_ anywhere in the title.

For example:

```
	[kitty]

	alt.] = C-tab
	alt.[ = C-S-tab
	alt.t = C-S-t

	[st-*]

	alt.1  = macro(Inside space st)

	[chromium]

	control.1 = macro(Inside space chrome!)
	alt.] = C-tab
	alt.[ = C-S-tab
	alt.t = C-t
```

The config maps _A-1_ to 'Inside st' when the active window's class begins with 'st-'.

Use _-v, --verbose_ to find class and title names.
When running in the background, read output with _tail\ -f\ ~/.config/keyd-rust/app.log_.
Config changes are loaded when window focus changes.
On X, GNOME and wlroots, send USR1 to refresh the current window's bindings.

The mapper supports X, KDE, GNOME, wlroots compositors such as Sway, and COSMIC.

# INSTALLATION

Start _keyd-rust-application-mapper -d_ from your desktop session startup,
such as _~/.xinitrc_ or _~/.xsession_. For GNOME, run the mapper first and follow
its instructions to install and enable the required extension.

keyd-rust must be running. Your user must have access to
*/var/run/keyd-rust.socket*, normally through the *keyd-rust* group.

# ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES

*KEYD_DEBUG*
	Debug log level. _0_,_1_ can be specified (default: 0).

# SECURITY

Grant access to */var/run/keyd-rust.socket* only to trusted users.
Treat membership in the _keyd-rust_ group as full access to the system.
